# Fresh authority stamp comparison

This finite nonproduct experiment compares eleven fresh Unix Stamp fields,
then the installed complete authority leaf validation method. It never grants
start authority, changes original windows or runs release qualification.

The frozen [protocol](protocol.json) specifies eight independent nonroot GNU
processes, twelve balanced three-arm samples and a same-function control.
`screen.rs` is the standalone prototype, not a runtime implementation. The
installed method lives in `diagnostic_authority_stamp_tests.rs` and has a manual,
non-ship gated-test registry entry. Run measurements only in an independently
approved isolated environment, never concurrently with compilation/tests.

Offline reader controls:

```text
python tools/authority-fresh-stamp-074/test_review.py
```

`review.py::review(cohorts, installed=False)` consumes the eight untouched stdout
byte streams. Set `installed=True` for exact libtest stdout. It validates the
original work count and labels before adapting records to the existing frozen
schedule/CPU estimator. Missing/reordered samples, changed work/clock values or
a wrong variant refuse. Negative estimates remain negative; admission is always
false. The synthetic controls are not benchmark observations.

The [result and evidence](../../docs/testing/performance/0.74/authority-fresh-stamp-result-20261025.md)
record both successful CPU screens and the first full preparation's expiry.
The leaf result must not be promoted into a full-preparation or product claim.
